sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Developer
    participant CLI as Rust CLI
    participant Journal as Journal file<br/>demo-01.json
    participant API as AnkiConnect
    participant Anki as Anki collection
    User->>CLI: create demo-01
    CLI->>Journal: lock state directory, load or save new UUID
    CLI->>API: readiness checks + findNotes(request tag)
    alt Exactly one existing match
        API-->>CLI: existing note ID
        CLI->>API: notesInfo + cardsInfo + uniqueness check
        CLI->>Journal: persist verified created_locally
    else Zero matches and journal is prepared
        CLI->>Journal: persist failed_unknown BEFORE HTTP write
        CLI->>API: addNote(fields, unique tag, duplicate check)
        API->>Anki: create note and generated cards
        alt Creation response received
            API-->>CLI: note ID
            CLI->>Journal: persist returned ID
        else Response lost or ambiguous
            API--xCLI: no usable creation result
            loop Bounded read-only reconciliation
                CLI->>API: readiness + findNotes(request tag)
                API-->>CLI: zero, one, or multiple IDs
            end
        end
        Note over CLI,Journal: Exactly one match is validated, zero/multiple stops without another addNote
        CLI->>API: notesInfo + cardsInfo + uniqueness check
        CLI->>Journal: created_locally only after successful validation
    else Multiple matches or previously attempted with zero matches
        Note over CLI: Stop, preserve journal for investigation
    end
